ers can=E2=80=99t turn the way that they=E2=80=99re drawn! However, the res=
olution here is simple:
we don=E2=80=99t draw any creases that would go through the overlap, except=
 the one where they agree. A region that cannot have creases through it is =
a <em>lake</em>.
This simplifies to the diagram on the right, where the overlap is replaced =
with
two new lakes we didn=E2=80=99t draw in the abstraction (but those lakes wi=
ll just be hidden, so it=E2=80=99s fine). A more formal proof that the over=
lap simplifies to those lakes
